{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The execution date is left in an illegible/incomplete form (\"September _/3 %\", 1973\") and the party defined as trustee is rendered only as a garbled word (\"truatae\"), so the identity of the defined term and the date of the instrument must be reconstructed. A court could be asked to fix the date of the trust and confirm that \"The First National Bank of Sullivan County ... Trust Department\" is the entity meant by \"Trustee\" throughout.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The written amount (\"Seventy-five and no/100 Dollars\") and the figure in parentheses (\"375.00\") do not agree, a mechanical error that changes the size of the initial corpus. A court would have to decide whether $75.00 or $375.00 was paid to the Trustee.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The bond's face amount is written as \"One Hundred and no/i00 Dollars ($100.09)\", the words and the numeral disagreeing, and the cash directed to be invested ($75 or $375 under I.A) does not match either. A court would have to construe what sum the Trustee was authorized to invest and in what denomination of bond.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The definition of \"Policies of Insurance\" is internally inconsistent — \"two (3) certificates\", the John Hancock policy attributed to a \"Tennessee Eastman Company\" group policy and the Metropolitan policy to Eastman Kodak, and both certificates given the identical number 819800. Because this defined term controls Articles I, II, III, IV and VI, a court would have to determine which policies actually fall within it.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.55}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The assignment operates only on \"the said Policies of Insurance\" as defined in I.B, so its reach depends entirely on that misdescribed definition and does not on its face reach substitute or successor group coverage that the attached Absolute Assignment (c034) purports to capture. A court would have to decide whether coverage issued in substitution for the named policies passed to the Trustee under this clause.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The reserved right to add is expressed in a mutilated sentence with words missing between \"from time [to time]\" and \"life which, when delivered to the Trustee\", leaving the class of addable property unstated. A court would have to supply what the Grantor reserved the right to add and on what terms it becomes trust property.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The vesting of \"all rights of absolute ownership\", including the power to surrender, cancel or convert the policies, cannot be squared with Article IV (c014), which says the Trustee \"shall be under no obligation or duty whatever except with respect to the safekeeping of the Policies of Insurance\". A court would have to decide whether the Trustee's ownership powers carry any correlative duty to preserve the coverage.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The clause makes the Trustee's receipts and releases \"binding and conclusive upon all persons interested in this trust\", which sits against Article XII (c031) making the Trustee answerable for its own bad faith or negligence. A court would have to decide whether beneficiaries are foreclosed by a trustee receipt from complaining of a negligent dealing with a policy.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This clause incorporates the attached assignment documents \"as fully as if set out verbatim\", importing terms — including the New York choice of law in the Metropolitan assignment (c038) — that conflict with Article XI (c030) making the trust governed by Tennessee law. A court would have to decide which incorporated terms control the trust relationship.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"All other instruments reasonably required\" gives no standard for what the Grantor may be compelled to sign, and the relinquishment is expressly conditional (\"if any such rights and powers exist\"). A court would have to determine what, if anything, this clause actually transferred.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.13}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
